The license check does more than validate a license:
- checkModuleStatus() calls Module\Status::setIsEnabled(), which rewrites the modules array in app/etc/config.php, and it runs from the extendware_core_cron job and from the admin config section.
- That file is per node while the config cache is shared, so nodes drift apart and serve configuration cached for a different module list.
- The call is redundant anyway: licensing is gated by extendware_module.module_active, which is what isModuleEnabled() reads.
Related tickets: IPET-3785

diff --git a/Model/Configure.php b/Model/Configure.php
--- a/Model/Configure.php
+++ b/Model/Configure.php
@@ -86,7 +86,9 @@
         curl_close($curl);
         $response = $response == 'true' ? true : false;

-        $this->status->setIsEnabled($response, [$extendwareModule->getModuleName()]);
+        // BEGIN PATCH
+        // $this->status->setIsEnabled($response, [$extendwareModule->getModuleName()]);
+        // END PATCH
         $extendwareModule->setModuleActive($response);
         $this->extendwareModuleRepository->save($extendwareModule);
         return $response;
